WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
Some patients can't speak, or even press a call button.

00:06.000 --> 00:08.000
Equal Care lets them ask for help with their eyes.

00:08.000 --> 00:10.000
Look left, right, up or down.

00:10.000 --> 00:14.000
One movement makes one selection.

00:18.000 --> 00:22.000
Inside a 145 × 110 × 38 mm enclosure with 2.8 mm walls,

00:22.000 --> 00:26.000
gel electrodes, a BioAmp Pill, an ESP32 and a battery pack.

00:26.000 --> 00:32.000
Click any part to see its name and what it does.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.000
Electrodes pick up the eye's electrical signal, called EOG.

00:36.000 --> 00:38.000
The BioAmp Pill amplifies it.

00:38.000 --> 00:44.000
The ESP32 sends the request over Wi-Fi to the staff dashboard.

00:44.000 --> 00:48.000
We calibrated it on real EOG recordings:

00:48.000 --> 00:54.000
raw signal, filtered signal and the direction of each movement.

00:54.000 --> 00:58.000
Here's a full request.

00:58.000 --> 01:00.000
The patient looks left to ask for water.

01:00.000 --> 01:04.000
It appears on the staff dashboard with a live timer.

01:04.000 --> 01:10.000
Staff acknowledge it, then resolve it.

01:10.000 --> 01:14.000
And the patient sees that help is coming.

01:16.000 --> 01:20.000
Equal Care.

01:20.000 --> 01:26.000
Built by OptiSync: Aarush, Kanika, Jiyaan and Avaneesh.
